// expect-error: T211
// Z3 corpus #28: axis-1 — Wall 4 Step 1 symbolic refinement RHS rejected.
//
// WHAT THIS FIXTURE PROVES
//
// V1's literal-only contract: refinement satisfiability is checked
// only when the field value is `TypedExpr::IntLiteral`. Symbolic values
// (function parameters, function-call results, destructured field
// reads) are explicitly deferred to a later step that adds fact
// propagation.
//
// The construction `Index { value: input }` supplies a symbolic value
// (the message handler parameter). Wall 4 Step 1 emits T211 without
// invoking Z3, with a hint instructing the agent to refactor into a
// literal-RHS construction or lift the symbolic value into a non-
// refined intermediate.
//
// THE LANGUAGE PRIMITIVES THIS NEEDED
//
// V1's containment is enforced in `check_record_refinements_at_construction`
// via `extract_int_literal`. A non-literal supplied value short-circuits
// the loop with T211 before any Z3 work happens — V11 dispatch is
// bypassed entirely because Z3 is never called.
//
// MUTATION CONTRACT
//
// Replacing `input` with a literal (e.g. `42`) would let Z3 run and
// (since 42 > 100 is false on the predicate `value > 100`) flip the
// fixture to a T210 case. Removing the refinement clause drops both
// T210 and T211 — the construction compiles.
module sigil;

record Index { value: i64 } where value > 100

entry actor Main {
    on Tick(input: i64) -> i64 {
        let idx: Index = Index { value: input };  // MUTATION_SITE
        return 1;
    }
}
